            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0524" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.4193/107: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-07T17:00:00+09:00">September 7, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 7—6:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>356. Our 327, August 29, 9 p.m., wounding of British Ambassador to China.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Provisional Japanese reply was handed yesterday to British Embassy and is
                        to the effect that up to the present investigations have failed to produce
                        any evidence that the shooting was done by a Japanese plane and that
                        consequently it is still impossible to determine whether the responsibility
                        rests with Japan.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>As text has been given to the press I shall not cable it unless
                        instructed.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for relay to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
